### Verdict: CHERRY_PICKING

### Justification
The fact-check confirmed that Taylor Zundel did post an Instagram video around October 27, 2020, about an incident during early voting in Utah, but a key detail in her claim was misleading: according to the [archived Herman Cain article](https://web.archive.org/web/20201119224000/https://hermancain.com/instagram-testimony-people-showing-vote-already-voted/), it was her **husband** and at least one other voter who were told they had already voted — not Zundel herself, who merely witnessed the event. Additionally, no official evidence of voter fraud was found; the source, a politically conservative blog, characterized the situation as either "bureaucratic incompetence... or fraud" without confirming either, and there is no independent verification from official Utah election records or mainstream news outlets to substantiate the specific incident. The verdict is **cherry-picking** because the claim misleadingly implies Zundel was personally affected when she was only a witness.